From: CervantesHallo <227578309+CervantesHallo@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: Clear DMO output status before requesting data.

The WMA DMO marks successful output INCOMPLETE to drain all packets. Its
next read can return MF_E_TRANSFORM_NEED_MORE_INPUT, which is converted to
S_FALSE. Leaving the previous flags in the reused descriptor makes the
DirectShow DMO wrapper drain empty buffers forever while holding stream_cs.
Stopping KiriKiri movie playback then blocks the game's UI thread.

Reset the output status before the read, including paths that are later
converted to S_FALSE. Keep valid output flags and buffer contents intact.
The same helper serves the other GStreamer-backed DMOs.

--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_sample.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_sample.c
@@ -492,6 +492,10 @@ HRESULT wg_transform_read_dmo(wg_transform_t transform, DMO_OUTPUT_DATA_BUFFER *buffer)
 
     TRACE_(mfplat)("transform %#I64x, buffer %p.\n", transform, buffer);
 
+    /* A failed read may become S_FALSE in the DMO. Do not retain flags
+     * from the preceding output, especially INCOMPLETE. */
+    buffer->dwStatus = 0;
+
     if (FAILED(hr = wg_sample_create_dmo(buffer->pBuffer, &wg_sample)))
         return hr;
     wg_sample->size = 0;
@@ -505,7 +509,6 @@ HRESULT wg_transform_read_dmo(wg_transform_t transform, DMO_OUTPUT_DATA_BUFFER *buffer)
         return hr;
     }
 
-    buffer->dwStatus = 0;
     if (wg_sample->flags & WG_SAMPLE_FLAG_INCOMPLETE)
         buffer->dwStatus |= DMO_OUTPUT_DATA_BUFFERF_INCOMPLETE;
     if (wg_sample->flags & WG_SAMPLE_FLAG_HAS_PTS)
